<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Stands in for a beach photo when there is no verified picture of that
  particular beach.

  Deliberately a drawing rather than a stock photograph: a generic photo in
  this slot would read as a picture *of this beach*, which is a claim the app
  cannot make. An illustration reads as "no photo yet" at a glance, and being
  drawn entirely from the palette it makes an unphotographed beach look like
  part of the app rather than a hole in it.

  Framed at 260x100 rather than the 2:1 the scene was drawn at, because the two
  slots it has to survive are different shapes: the detail card is about 2:1 and
  a nearby-beach row is nearer 3:1, and both use centerCrop. So the sky, sea and
  sand run edge to edge while every object - sun, clouds, gulls, kite, umbrella,
  ball - is kept inside x 12%-88% and y 10%-90%, the window that survives the
  worst crop either slot can ask for. Nothing that reads as a thing gets cut.

  Colours come from placeholder_* tokens, which have an after-dark set in
  values-night. Which set is used is decided by BeachPlaceholder from sunrise
  and sunset at the beach's own coordinates, not from the phone's theme, so a
  beach is drawn the way it would actually look right now.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="260dp"
    android:height="100dp"
    android:viewportWidth="260"
    android:viewportHeight="100">

